        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Madman's Return, \"Rhythm Is a Dancer\", \"Colour of Love\"\n- People: Turbo B\n- Organizations: Snap!\n- Topics: chart performance, music releases\n\nFacts:\n- Turbo B, born Durron Maurice Butler on April 30, 1967, is an American musician, rapper, and beatboxer known for fronting Snap!.\n- \"Colour of Love\" was released in December 1991 as the first single from Snap!'s second studio album, The Madman's Return.\n- The Madman's Return is Snap!'s second studio album.\n- \"Rhythm Is a Dancer\" is a song recorded by the German group Snap!.\n- The Madman's Return contains the international hit \"Rhythm Is a Dancer\".\n- \"Rhythm Is a Dancer\" reached number 1 in France, Ireland, Italy, the Netherlands, Germany, and the United Kingdom.\n- \"Rhythm Is a Dancer\" peaked at number 5 in the United States.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
